Critical preparation and fitting failures are silently downgraded to coverage insufficiency, allowing an invalid integration run to appear successfully frozen and replayed. Review was read-only; computing artifacts and unrelated work were not inspected.

Review comment:

- [P1] Propagate critical preparation and fitting errors — /home/drwho1985/workspace/algotradinglife/beijing-lot/r/fm_lambda_integration_freeze.R:105-108
  If preparation or fitting raises a critical contract, cutoff-binding, implementation-verification, environment, or unexpected runtime error, this catch converts it into `UNESTIMATED` and retains the parent probabilities. The batch can consequently freeze and replay successfully without distinguishing broken execution from expected insufficient history. Catch only explicitly recognized insufficiency failures and rethrow everything else; add tests covering both paths. [AGENTS.md:56–57](AGENTS.md#L56-L57) requires critical boundary failures to stop.
